// Barks (doc 94): the host side of the lines over the head. Every Life frame the engine (internal/barks, generated from
// world.barks) reads the people of the hero's level — where they stand, whether they sit on a stool or stand on their
// post — and the world facts, and picks at most one line per place by period, facts, cooldown, the place's silence and
// weight, deterministically by seed; an answer follows after its delay. The client gets the localized text, the face of
// the speaker's caste and the clock of the line, and only draws it. The clocks are saved with the game.
// The fighting layer speaks through BarkEvent / BarkCue (owner 02.11): without its calls a fight stays silent.
